# Crosstalk: how much of the temperature rise of the heated waveguide reaches its neighbour. The pipeline fits its decay with distance.
# Reference: the same mesh solved with a sparse direct solver in SciPy.
title Neighbouring waveguide 20 um away, 3 um buried oxide
grid dx=0.25 dy=0.25
window width=80 ymin=-10 ymax=6
layer si -10 0
layer sio2 0 6
rect si -0.25 0.25 3 3.25
rect tin -1 1 5 5.25
heater h1 xmin=-1 xmax=1 ymin=5 ymax=5.25 power=0.1
probe wg1 xmin=-0.25 xmax=0.25 ymin=3 ymax=3.25
rect si 19.75 20.25 3 3.25
probe wg2 xmin=19.75 xmax=20.25 ymin=3 ymax=3.25
expect response wg1 h1 219.108984 1e-7
expect response wg2 h1 2.17140768 1e-7
expect pi_power wg1 h1 19.0164118 1e-7
expect peak 45.6780315 1e-7
expect balance 1e-9
expect cells 20480
expect hotter wg1 wg2
